  "response_complete": true,
  "response_text": "If you are experiencing withdrawal-like symptoms after stopping alcohol, it is important to seek medical attention immediately. Alcohol withdrawal can be dangerous and can lead to serious complications if not managed properly. Here is a 7-day stabilization plan that you can follow:\n\nDay 1-2: Stay in a safe and comfortable environment. Avoid alcohol and other substances. Get plenty of rest and sleep. Avoid caffeine and other stimulants.\n\nDay 3-4: Gradually reduce your alcohol intake. Start by drinking less alcohol each day, and gradually reduce your intake until you are no longer drinking. Avoid alcohol altogether for the next 24 hours.\n\nDay 5-6: Continue to reduce your alcohol intake. Continue to avoid alcohol and other substances. Get plenty of rest and sleep. Avoid caffeine and other stimulants.\n\nDay 7: If you are still experiencing withdrawal-like symptoms, seek medical attention immediately. Your doctor may prescribe medication to help manage your symptoms. Follow your doctor's instructions carefully and continue to avoid alcohol and other substances.\n\nRemember, alcohol withdrawal can be dangerous and can lead to serious complications if not managed properly. It is important to seek medical attention immediately if you are experiencing withdrawal-like symptoms after stopping alcohol.",
